-- Performance (Time-Series)
CREATE TABLE portfolio_performance (
    performance_id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    account_id UUID,
    performance_date DATE,
    period_return DECIMAL(10,4),
    cumulative_return DECIMAL(10,4),
    portfolio_value DECIMAL(18,2),
    contributions DECIMAL(18,2),
    withdrawals DECIMAL(18,2),
    fees DECIMAL(18,2),
    INDEX idx_perf_account_date (account_id, performance_date)
);
```

### 2.2 Database Design Principles

**Normalization:**
- Third Normal Form (3NF) for transactional data
- Denormalization for read-heavy data (performance reporting)
- Document storage (MongoDB/PostgreSQL JSONB) for flexible data

**Indexing Strategy:**
- Primary keys: Automatic indexes
- Foreign keys: Performance queries (account_id, household_id)
- Time-series data: Date/time indexes
- Search fields: Full-text indexes on client names
- Composite indexes for common query patterns

**Partitioning:**
- Audit logs: Partitioned by month
- Performance data: Partitioned by account and date
- Trade history: Partitioned by year

**Data Retention:**
- Transactional data: 7+ years (regulatory requirement)
- Audit logs: 7 years
- Session data: 1 year
- Temporary cache: 24 hours

